# Backend — Skills & Conventions

## Before writing

1. Read relevant area docs before modifying backend code.
2. Apply the cross-cutting code-quality skills → see `.claude/rules/code-quality.md` (`clean-code`, `test-driven-development`, `verification-before-completion`).

## Core skill

**[SKILL_BACKEND]** — always active for backend work (middleware, routing, error handling).

## Skills — invoke BEFORE the edit, not after it bounces (LAW10)

Each skill below has a concrete trigger. When your work matches it, invoke the skill
(Skill tool) BEFORE the first hand-edit — not after a hand-patch fails. **Hand-editing
an area a skill covers twice without loading it = you already skipped it (LAW10): stop
and load it now.**

